IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for qld-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the text of the Act, as cited, before the file was run.

§ `Tests of the time rules`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no holidays and no closed offices` MEANS `Facts about the days of a place` WITH
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS EMPTY
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS EMPTY

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`a period of days` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of days`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`a period of weeks` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of weeks`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`a period of months` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of calendar months`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`a period of years` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of years`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
`the beginning of` MEANS `the beginning of a day` (Date d m y)

§§ `Moments: Schedule 1 midnight, s 15B, s 18`

-- SAYS The midnight of a day is the point of time at which the day ends, which is the same point of time as the beginning of the next day (Schedule 1, midnight).
-- Schedule 1, midnight: the point of time at which the day ends.  The end of 1 January 2026 is the beginning of 2 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` (`midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 1 2026)) (`the beginning of a day` (Date 2 1 2026))
#ASSERT NOT `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` (`midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 1 2026)) (`the beginning of a day` (Date 1 1 2026))
#ASSERT `the first moment is before the second moment` (`the beginning of a day` (Date 1 1 2026)) (`midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 1 2026))
#ASSERT NOT `the first moment is before the second moment` (`the beginning of a day` (Date 2 1 2026)) (`midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 1 2026))

-- s 15B: a provision that commences on a day commences at the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)` (Date 12 4 1995) EQUALS `the beginning of` 12 4 1995
#ASSERT `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` (`the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)` (Date 12 4 1995)) (`the beginning of a day` (Date 12 4 1995))

-- s 18: a provision that expires on a day, or remains in force until a day, has effect until the end of the day.
#ASSERT `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` (`the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)` (Date 30 6 2026)) (`the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026))
#ASSERT `the first moment is before the second moment` (`the beginning of a day` (Date 30 6 2026)) (`the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)` (Date 30 6 2026))

§§ `Commencement: ss 15A, 15C(1), 15D, 22C(1)`

-- s 15A: an Act commences on the date of assent except so far as it otherwise expressly provides.
#ASSERT `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 5 4 1995)
#ASSERT `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` (Date 5 4 1995) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 15C(1): the citation and commencement provisions commence on the date of assent, at the beginning of that day (s 15B).
#ASSERT `the moment the citation and commencement provisions of an Act commence (s 15C(1))` (Date 5 4 1995) EQUALS `the beginning of` 5 4 1995

-- SAYS If the day fixed by a proclamation for the commencement of an Act or provision comes before the day on which the proclamation is notified, the Act or provision commences on the notification day (s 15D(2)).
-- s 15D(2): a day fixed before the notification day does not bring the commencement forward; the Act commences on the notification day.
#ASSERT `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 20 3 2026

-- SAYS An amending Act enacted after 30 June 1994 is automatically repealed at the beginning of the day after all of its provisions have commenced (s 22C(1)).
-- s 22C(1) and its Example 1: repealing provisions commence on assent, 21 March 1995; amending provisions on proclamation, 12 April 1995;
-- the amending Act is automatically repealed at the beginning of 13 April 1995.
#ASSERT `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (Date 21 3 1995) TRUE (Date 12 4 1995) EQUALS JUST (`the beginning of` 13 4 1995)
-- Example 2: an Act containing scheme provisions is not an amending Act covered by subsection (1).
#ASSERT `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (Date 21 3 1995) FALSE (Date 12 4 1995) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "enacted after 30 June 1994": assent on 30 June 1994 is not after; 1 July 1994 is.
#ASSERT `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (Date 30 6 1994) TRUE (Date 12 4 1995) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (Date 1 7 1994) TRUE (Date 31 12 1994) EQUALS JUST (`the beginning of` 1 1 1995)

§§ `Postponed laws: s 15DA`

-- SAYS A postponed law enacted after 31 December 1994 that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day automatically commences on the next day, and a regulation made within that year may extend the period to not more than 2 years of the assent day (s 15DA(2), (3) and (5)).
-- The Example in s 15DA: assent 5 April 1995; not commenced by 5 April 1996, so it commences on 6 April 1996.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 6 4 1996)
-- (3): a regulation made within the year extends the period to not more than 2 years of the assent day: to 5 April 1997, so 6 April 1997.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 24 EQUALS JUST (Date 6 4 1997)
-- An extension to 13 months from 6 April 1995 ends on 5 May 1996, so commencement is on 6 May 1996.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 13 EQUALS JUST (Date 6 5 1996)
-- More than 2 years is not authorised by (3); a figure of 12 or less is not an extension.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 25 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(a): only a postponed law enacted after 31 December 1994.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 31 12 1994) FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 1 1 1995) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 1996)
-- (5)(b): unless an Act expressly states it does not apply.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 5 4 1995) TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Assent on 29 February 1996: the year runs from 1 March 1996 to 28 February 1997; commencement on 1 March 1997.
#ASSERT `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` (Date 29 2 1996) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 1997)

§§ `Schedule 1: calendar month, calendar year, financial year`

-- SAYS A calendar month starting at the beginning of a day ends immediately before the beginning of the corresponding day of the next named month, or, if there is no such day, at the end of the next named month (Schedule 1, calendar month).
-- A month starting on the 1st of February 2024 ends immediately before the beginning of 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- Starting on the 31st: there is no 31 February, so the month ends at the end of February.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 30 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 29 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- Starting on the 29th of January 2024: 29 February 2024 exists, so the month ends immediately before it.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 29 1 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2024
-- Starting on the 28th of January 2025: 28 February 2025 exists.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 28 1 2025) EQUALS Date 27 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS Date 14 2 2025
-- A month starting on 31 December: the next named month is January, which has a 31st.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 30 1 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- A month starting on 31 March: April has no 31st.
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` (Date 30 11 2025) EQUALS Date 29 12 2025

-- Months in succession: each starts at the beginning of the day after the last ended.
#ASSERT `the last day of calendar months in succession` 1 (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of calendar months in succession` 2 (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS Date 31 3 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of calendar months in succession` 2 (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026

-- SAYS A calendar year is a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January, and a financial year is a period of 1 year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1, calendar year and financial year).
-- Schedule 1, calendar year: a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January.
#ASSERT `the first day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` 2025 EQUALS Date 1 1 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` 2025 EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` 2024 EQUALS Date 31 12 2024
-- Schedule 1, financial year: a period of 1 year beginning on 1 July.
#ASSERT `the last day of the financial year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1)` 2025 EQUALS Date 30 6 2026

§§ `Periods: s 38(1)`

-- SAYS A period beginning on a given day, act or event is calculated by excluding that day, or the day of the act or event (s 38(1)).
-- The worked cases.  Each is the last day of the period before s 38(2) is applied.
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: the 1st is excluded, so day 1 is 2 January and day 30 is 31 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of days` 30) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: the month starts at the beginning of 1 February and ends at the end of 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 31 1 2024) (`a period of months` 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025: January, then February; the last day is 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 31 12 2025) (`a period of months` 2) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- One year from 29 February 2024, read as 12 calendar months from 1 March 2024: the last day is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 29 2 2024) (`a period of years` 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: 36 calendar months from 17 July 2025, ending 16 July 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 16 7 2025) (`a period of years` 3) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025 and from 1 September 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 15 1 2025) (`a period of years` 5) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 9 2025) (`a period of years` 5) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- Other days and months.
-- Two months from 30 January 2025: the first month begins on 31 January and, as there is no 31 February, ends at the end of February (28 February); the second runs from 1 March to 31 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 30 1 2025) (`a period of months` 2) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 31 12 2025) (`a period of days` 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 15 1 2025) (`a period of months` 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 30 1 2025) (`a period of months` 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- SAYS The Act does not define "week", so it does not say how long a period of weeks is, and a period of weeks is not answered (silent).
-- A period of weeks: the Act does not define "week".  A period of fewer than one: not covered.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of weeks` 2) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of days` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of months` 0) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38(1): the given day is excluded; the day after it is the first day counted.
#ASSERT NOT `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2025)

-- SAYS For a period expressed as a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is excluded as well; in any other case it is included (s 38(1)(a) and (b)).
-- s 38(1)(a): clear days (or at least a number of days) also exclude the day on which the purpose is fulfilled.
#ASSERT `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 38(1)(b): in any other case it is included.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the purpose can be fulfilled within days (s 38(1)(b))` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day on which the purpose can be fulfilled within days (s 38(1)(b))` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is counted in the period (s 38(1)(a) and (b))` `a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days`
#ASSERT `the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is counted in the period (s 38(1)(a) and (b))` `any other period`

-- s 38(1) and (3): backwards, the given day is excluded and the earliest day is n days before it.
#ASSERT `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))` (Date 10 3 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))` (Date 10 3 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Excluded days and the move off them: s 38(2), (3), (5), Schedule 1 business day`

`Christmas Day 2026 and the Monday after` MEANS `Facts about the days of a place` WITH
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS EMPTY
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS LIST (Date 25 12 2026), (Date 28 12 2026)

`an office closed on a Saturday and Sunday` MEANS `Facts about the days of a place` WITH
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS LIST (Date 31 1 2026), (Date 1 2 2026)
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS EMPTY

`a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026` MEANS `Facts about the days of a place` WITH
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS EMPTY
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS LIST (Date 2 2 2026)

-- SAYS A business day is a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday and not a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday in the place in which any relevant act is to be or may be done (Schedule 1, business day).
-- Schedule 1, business day: not a Saturday or Sunday, and not a holiday in the place.
#ASSERT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (Date 2 2 2026) `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT NOT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (Date 31 1 2026) `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT NOT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (Date 1 2 2026) `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT NOT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (Date 2 2 2026) `a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026`
#ASSERT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (Date 3 2 2026) `a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026`

-- SAYS For filing or registering a document an excluded day is a day on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done; otherwise it is a day that is not a business day in the place in which the thing must or may be done (s 38(5)).
-- s 38(5)(b): otherwise, a day that is not a business day.
#ASSERT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 31 1 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT NOT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 2 2 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 2 2 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026`
-- s 38(5)(a): for filing or registering, a day on which the office is closed.  A Saturday on which the office is open is not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 31 1 2026) `filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices`
#ASSERT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 31 1 2026) `filing or registering a document` `an office closed on a Saturday and Sunday`
#ASSERT NOT `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` (Date 2 2 2026) `filing or registering a document` `a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026`

-- SAYS If the time, or last day of a period, calculated forwards for doing anything falls on an excluded day, it is taken to fall on the next later day that is not an excluded day (s 38(2)).
-- s 38(2): the last day of thirty days from 1 January 2026 is Saturday 31 January 2026, an excluded day; the next later day that is not excluded is Monday 2 February.
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 31 1 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- Monday 2 February 2026 a holiday: Tuesday 3 February.
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 31 1 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `a holiday on Monday 2 February 2026` EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
-- A day that is not excluded stays where it is.
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 29 2 2024) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- Filing, with the office open on the Saturday: the day stays; closed on the weekend: Monday.
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 31 1 2026) `filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS Date 31 1 2026
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 31 1 2026) `filing or registering a document` `an office closed on a Saturday and Sunday` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- Friday 25 December 2026 a holiday, then the weekend, then Monday 28 December a holiday: Tuesday 29 December.
#ASSERT `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (Date 25 12 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `Christmas Day 2026 and the Monday after` EQUALS Date 29 12 2026
-- SAYS If the time, or earliest day of a period, calculated backwards for doing anything falls on an excluded day, it is taken to fall on the next earlier day that is not an excluded day (s 38(3)).
-- s 38(3): backwards, Sunday 1 February 2026 moves to Friday 30 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` (Date 1 2 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS Date 30 1 2026
#ASSERT `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` (Date 3 2 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
-- Monday 28 December 2026 a holiday, backwards: Friday 25 December also a holiday, so Thursday 24 December.
#ASSERT `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` (Date 28 12 2026) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `Christmas Day 2026 and the Monday after` EQUALS Date 24 12 2026

§§ `The worked cases with s 38(2) applied (no holidays, nothing closed)`

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: last day Saturday 31 January 2026; moved to Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of days` 30) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 for filing, office open on the Saturday: stays on 31 January.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of days` 30) `filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: Thursday 29 February 2024, not excluded.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 31 1 2024) (`a period of months` 1) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025: Saturday 28 February 2026, moved to Monday 2 March 2026.  The rest-day rule is applied to a period in months.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 31 12 2025) (`a period of months` 2) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: Friday 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 29 2 2024) (`a period of years` 1) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: Sunday 16 July 2028, moved to Monday 17 July 2028.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 16 7 2025) (`a period of years` 3) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025: Tuesday 15 January 2030.  From 1 September 2025: Sunday 1 September 2030, moved to Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 15 1 2025) (`a period of years` 5) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 1 9 2025) (`a period of years` 5) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- A period of weeks stays not covered after the move.
#ASSERT `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` (Date 1 1 2026) (`a period of weeks` 1) `anything other than filing or registering a document` `no holidays and no closed offices` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `No time provided: s 38(4)`

-- SAYS If no time is provided or allowed for doing anything, the thing is to be done as soon as possible, and as often as the relevant occasion happens (s 38(4)).
#ASSERT `when a thing is to be done if no time is provided (s 38(4))` FALSE EQUALS JUST `as soon as possible, and as often as the relevant occasion happens`
#ASSERT `when a thing is to be done if no time is provided (s 38(4))` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Age: s 38A`

-- SAYS A person is an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for the age (s 38A).
-- Born 10 May 2008: 17 on the 9th of May 2026, 18 at the beginning of the birthday.
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 10 5 2008) (Date 9 5 2026) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 10 5 2008) (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 10 5 2008) (Date 11 5 2026) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 10 5 2008) (Date 10 5 2008) EQUALS JUST 0
-- A day before the date of birth: not covered.
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 10 5 2008) (Date 9 5 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Born 29 February 2008.  In a leap year the birthday is 29 February.
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST 16
-- In a year with no 29 February the Act does not say whether the birthday is 28 February or 1 March.
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST 18

§§ `Service by post: s 39A(1)`

-- SAYS Service by post is taken to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved; once the contrary is proved the Act gives no time (s 39A(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` (`the beginning of` 6 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the beginning of` 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` (`the beginning of` 6 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Acting appointments: s 24B(5) and (6)`

-- SAYS The term of an acting appointment made because of a vacancy may not be more than 1 year (s 24B(5)(a)).
-- A term beginning 1 March 2026 may run to the end of 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the latest last day of the term of an acting appointment because of a vacancy (s 24B(5))` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- A vacancy on 29 February 2024: a year from that day ends 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day an appointee may continue to act at the end of a year from the day of the vacancy (s 24B(6)(c))` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the last day an appointee may continue to act at the end of a year from the day of the vacancy (s 24B(6)(c))` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2027
